WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.007
[theme music playing]

01:03.313 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:08.902 --> 01:10.111
If that's your plan,

01:11.279 --> 01:12.989
why not just scrap the wishes

01:13.698 --> 01:15.784
and throw me off right now?

01:16.493 --> 01:17.410
I'm having…

01:18.787 --> 01:20.789
[laughing] …an absolute blast right now!

01:20.872 --> 01:22.874
[laughing]

01:24.876 --> 01:26.002
You're enjoying this?

01:26.086 --> 01:27.253
Yes.

01:28.088 --> 01:30.006
I was so bored with life,

01:30.089 --> 01:33.843
but my heart is racing
right now. [choking]

01:35.845 --> 01:38.389
-This is fun?
-[laughing]

01:40.266 --> 01:43.186
[Iblis] Fine.
Let me kick things up a notch.

01:43.269 --> 01:45.271
[tense music plays]

01:48.441 --> 01:49.859
[Ka-young choking]

01:58.993 --> 02:00.411
[laughing]

02:11.214 --> 02:13.091
-[chokes]
-[sniffs]

02:15.468 --> 02:16.302
It is you.

02:18.596 --> 02:19.931
That lump of clay.

02:20.974 --> 02:22.100
I'm sure of it.

02:28.273 --> 02:29.816
I guess I've been too complacent.

02:31.151 --> 02:33.611
Is this how corrupt humans have become?

02:34.863 --> 02:36.865
Are you humans already beyond temptation?

02:37.907 --> 02:40.326
How was it when you fell?
Did you feel any pain?

02:42.120 --> 02:43.413
Let me in on your plans.

02:43.496 --> 02:46.583
While you're trying to kill me,
can I try to kill you too?

02:49.169 --> 02:51.796
[grunts, coughs]

02:53.715 --> 02:54.924
I'm warning you.

02:55.967 --> 02:57.969
Lay a finger on me again,

02:59.053 --> 03:00.930
and I will wipe out your entire kind,

03:01.556 --> 03:03.558
every single being apart from you,

03:04.434 --> 03:05.852
from the elderly to infants.

03:07.061 --> 03:09.647
I will exterminate every last being,

03:10.690 --> 03:11.816
sparing no one…

03:14.068 --> 03:16.029
if that's what it takes
to watch you suffer.

03:19.532 --> 03:22.577
For 983 years,
you've been part of my plans.

03:25.371 --> 03:26.205
[Ka-young] Wait.

03:27.206 --> 03:28.917
You're just leaving me here?

03:29.000 --> 03:30.960
[yelling] How am I supposed to get down?

03:47.018 --> 03:48.853
Four wheels? Ha!

03:50.688 --> 03:53.650
Must be the things Sade mentioned
that walk around on their own.

03:54.317 --> 03:57.320
-[people exclaiming]
-[growling]

03:59.489 --> 04:00.865
[growling]

04:03.201 --> 04:05.703
[chattering, exclaiming]

04:06.537 --> 04:08.539
[Sade snarls]

04:10.416 --> 04:12.377
-[snarls]
-[people gasp, exclaim]

04:21.010 --> 04:23.304
My mythical beast, Sade.

04:26.266 --> 04:27.100
[Sade] Master?

04:27.183 --> 04:29.269
When did you get out here?

04:29.936 --> 04:31.020
Get out.

04:31.104 --> 04:34.691
[Sade] There are a lot of eyes
on me right now,

04:34.774 --> 04:36.609
so I'll meet you over at the oasis.

04:36.693 --> 04:37.777
I'll see you later.

04:37.860 --> 04:40.321
I've changed a lot,
so try not to be too alarmed.

04:41.030 --> 04:42.824
Get over here this instant!

04:44.325 --> 04:47.620
[Sade] I was born
of a single glistening tear

04:47.704 --> 04:51.040
shed on a strand
of my master's silky raven hair.

04:51.916 --> 04:56.629
If you hear what I am saying now
in your native language, that's because--

04:56.713 --> 04:59.132
What are you mumbling about?
Get your ass over here!

04:59.215 --> 05:04.053
[growls] It's been far too long.
I've missed you, Master. [sniffing]

05:04.137 --> 05:06.556
Oh. Master's scent. [growls]

05:07.098 --> 05:10.351
Cut it out. You seemed
perfectly happy serving other masters.

05:10.435 --> 05:12.812
I was only doing what I had to.
Take a look.

05:12.895 --> 05:16.316
Even the oasis
has become a luxurious hotel.

05:18.109 --> 05:22.530
Animal protection laws prohibit hunting,
so I'm practically a herbivore now.

05:32.165 --> 05:33.583
By the way, did you get hurt?

05:33.666 --> 05:36.044
Earlier, I felt my head splitting
and my back breaking.

05:37.462 --> 05:39.172
There was a bit of a situation.

05:41.215 --> 05:44.385
Don't tell me banging my head
made your face so…

05:44.469 --> 05:45.970
What about my face?

05:46.554 --> 05:48.306
Right, you haven't seen me like this.

05:48.389 --> 05:50.975
This is the face
I mentioned taking a liking to.

05:52.435 --> 05:53.269
What?

05:53.352 --> 05:55.980
[sighs] Where should I even start
bringing you up to speed?

05:56.064 --> 05:58.775
Anyway, so you finally have a new master.

05:58.858 --> 06:01.069
Well? Do they look like
they'd have a lot of wishes?

06:01.152 --> 06:02.153
No.

06:02.820 --> 06:04.864
She says she doesn't need any wishes.

06:05.448 --> 06:06.949
It's honestly so strange.

06:17.752 --> 06:18.586
[door opens]

06:22.340 --> 06:25.676
-[passenger humming]
-[watch ticking]

06:53.287 --> 06:55.873
[humming]

06:57.583 --> 06:59.252
-You're in my seat.
-Hmm.

07:00.336 --> 07:02.922
This is my first time
riding a carpet like this one.

07:03.005 --> 07:05.550
And this. It's so delicious. [chuckles]

07:06.926 --> 07:10.388
-You abandoned me in your hotel.
-I didn't abandon you. I left you there.

07:10.471 --> 07:12.932
-Yeah, you abandoned me.
-No, I left you there.

07:15.101 --> 07:16.644
Will we ever have a proper chat?

07:17.228 --> 07:19.605
I already told you.
I can't leave your side.

07:21.482 --> 07:23.276
I'm saying stop wasting your time.

07:24.402 --> 07:25.695
[yawns]

07:27.238 --> 07:29.866
I feel drowsy after the meal.
See you in Goryeo.

07:31.617 --> 07:33.995
-[comical music plays]
-[Iblis humming]

07:35.830 --> 07:37.540
What a pain in the ass.

07:38.666 --> 07:40.001
We'll talk later.

07:41.294 --> 07:43.754
For now, our hairstyles
are way too similar.

07:43.838 --> 07:46.632
Stop wearing it in a bun,
or shave your head already.

07:46.716 --> 07:49.218
I busted my ass with hair masks
to grow this out,

07:49.302 --> 07:51.345
so you change yours! You hear me?

07:57.018 --> 07:59.187
[Ok-nam] Mm. We want them nice and crispy.

07:59.270 --> 08:00.521
[Ka-young] I'm home.

08:01.731 --> 08:02.565
My word.

08:04.567 --> 08:05.401
What is it?

08:05.485 --> 08:07.904
Ka-young, I thought
you were glowing lately.

08:07.987 --> 08:09.697
It must be because you're dating.

08:09.780 --> 08:11.365
I don't date.

08:11.449 --> 08:12.909
I've just always been pretty.

08:12.992 --> 08:13.826
Then

08:14.827 --> 08:16.662
who is that lanky man with you?

08:17.622 --> 08:19.123
-[comical music plays]
-Ah.

08:23.044 --> 08:25.296
Don't say a word. Not a single word.

08:27.089 --> 08:28.216
He's just a souvenir.

08:28.966 --> 08:30.259
That's Granny An,

08:30.760 --> 08:31.677
Granny Park,

08:32.178 --> 08:33.221
Granny Sa,

08:33.804 --> 08:34.722
and my grandma.

08:34.805 --> 08:37.517
[Heung-rye] Goodness, this is incredible.

08:37.600 --> 08:40.520
She went overseas
and brought back a potential husband.

08:40.603 --> 08:42.438
He's not a potential husband.

08:42.522 --> 08:43.439
We're just

08:44.273 --> 08:45.233
sharing a room.

08:45.316 --> 08:46.400
What?

08:46.484 --> 08:48.569
Well, if you share a room,

08:48.653 --> 08:51.239
who's to say, you know?

08:51.322 --> 08:53.074
Who knows what might happen?

08:53.157 --> 08:55.701
Pan-geum, you'll have
great-grandchildren in no time.

08:55.785 --> 08:58.329
-[Bok-ja] Come on, stop that.
-[laughing]

08:59.247 --> 09:01.040
Have you eaten? [laughs]

09:01.666 --> 09:03.918
Welcome. I'm An Bok-ja.

09:04.001 --> 09:07.380
Right, well, I think Lee Beul-li
will be a suitable name for me.

09:07.463 --> 09:08.464
"Lee Beul-li"?

09:09.507 --> 09:10.800
[both] Lee Beul-li?

09:12.593 --> 09:13.678
[Ka-young] Follow me.

09:14.971 --> 09:18.391
Goodness, why take a detour to the shed
before going inside?

09:18.474 --> 09:21.102
-[laughs]
-Enough of that!

09:21.185 --> 09:23.729
What are you doing?
It'll burn. Hurry up and flip it!

09:23.813 --> 09:25.022
It's cooked perfectly.

09:26.983 --> 09:27.942
"Lee Beul-li"?

09:30.778 --> 09:32.321
I did some research.

09:32.405 --> 09:34.740
Everyone here has three-character names.

09:35.241 --> 09:36.951
An Bok-ja. Ki Ka-young.

09:37.660 --> 09:38.661
Lee Beul-li.

09:39.370 --> 09:41.664
It makes sense. I'll give you that.

09:41.747 --> 09:42.915
But…

09:44.792 --> 09:46.586
Never mind. Whatever works for you.

09:47.378 --> 09:50.590
All right, ground rules.
Stay out of sight of the grannies.

09:50.673 --> 09:52.800
And definitely stay
out of sight of the locals.

09:52.883 --> 09:55.928
No going into town.
No getting caught using magic.

09:56.012 --> 09:58.306
No telling me to make a wish.

09:58.848 --> 09:59.765
[in English] Okay?

10:00.391 --> 10:01.684
[in Korean] Then, what can I do?

10:02.852 --> 10:05.771
I came all this way, and for what?
You want to kill me?

10:05.855 --> 10:08.858
If that's what you desire, wish it.
It's simple.

10:08.941 --> 10:11.736
Why would I use a wish on that?
I could do it myself.

10:16.699 --> 10:18.743
What are you yapping about to yourself?

10:20.411 --> 10:22.246
Where did that lanky fellow go?

10:23.873 --> 10:25.708
-Why the pickax?
-[chuckles softly]

10:28.127 --> 10:29.462
Only I can see you again?

10:29.545 --> 10:31.047
You said to avoid the grannies.

10:32.340 --> 10:33.424
[Pan-geum] What is it?

10:33.507 --> 10:34.842
Are you seeing things?

10:34.925 --> 10:36.344
Did you skip your meds?

10:36.427 --> 10:37.887
[sighs heavily]

10:39.680 --> 10:40.514
Cover your ears.

10:41.641 --> 10:42.975
Maybe I'll just kill this--

10:43.059 --> 10:45.144
Kill what? Who are you going to kill?

10:45.227 --> 10:47.855
Ka-young, you remember
your promise to me, right?

10:47.938 --> 10:49.023
Remember our rules?

10:58.699 --> 10:59.700
-[pickax clangs]
-I do.

11:00.534 --> 11:02.662
-[ticking]
-[breathing deeply]

11:20.930 --> 11:24.809
Your mom, dad, and older sisters

11:24.892 --> 11:26.435
aren't coming back.

11:27.353 --> 11:28.270
They're all dead.

11:29.063 --> 11:30.314
But how did they die?

11:30.398 --> 11:32.566
I only killed Mom's parrot.

11:33.234 --> 11:35.403
Mom, Dad, and my older sisters.

11:35.486 --> 11:36.529
I didn't kill them.

11:36.612 --> 11:38.072
Of course you didn't.

11:38.572 --> 11:40.366
Grandma knows you didn't.

11:41.117 --> 11:44.495
And you won't kill anyone
in the future either.

11:44.995 --> 11:46.705
And no killing birds either.

11:47.289 --> 11:50.084
Let's live a long life together,
me and you, okay?

11:52.086 --> 11:53.712
But they said they'd come back.

11:53.796 --> 11:56.465
They promised. [panting]

11:57.925 --> 12:01.053
So why are they dead?
How could they die without my permission?

12:01.137 --> 12:03.806
[panting]

12:14.692 --> 12:15.609
[ticking]

12:15.693 --> 12:18.654
From now on,
this is what you do when you're angry.

12:19.697 --> 12:23.367
Close your eyes and listen to the watch.
It goes ticktock, doesn't it?

12:23.951 --> 12:27.955
Let's listen to that sound 60 times
and try to hold it in for one minute.

12:28.539 --> 12:30.082
I don't want to. Get off me.

12:30.166 --> 12:32.168
I'm still angry, so what now?

12:32.251 --> 12:34.753
Then you should listen for two minutes.

12:34.837 --> 12:36.464
Let's try it, okay?

12:37.381 --> 12:38.466
No!

12:38.549 --> 12:40.551
Just put it away! Get rid of it!

12:40.634 --> 12:43.721
[panting] Get rid of it already! Now!

12:44.221 --> 12:47.933
I don't want this! [panting heavily]

12:48.017 --> 12:50.019
KA-YOUNG'S STUDY COMPILATION 1

12:50.102 --> 12:53.731
-[Ka-young counting]
-Mr. Chang-sik made this for you.

12:53.814 --> 12:55.274
Shall we take a look?

12:55.357 --> 12:58.027
Oh my, this looks like fun.
Don't you think?

12:58.110 --> 13:00.070
[nurse] Congratulations.
You have a baby girl.

13:00.154 --> 13:01.864
-Chae-a.
-My goodness.

13:01.947 --> 13:04.033
-Our precious princess!
-It's me, Dad.

13:04.116 --> 13:05.618
[Pan-geum] See that, Ka-young?

13:05.701 --> 13:09.205
That dad and grandma
look incredibly happy, don't they?

13:09.705 --> 13:12.124
That is real joy.

13:12.208 --> 13:15.794
766 seconds, 767 seconds, 768 seconds,

13:15.878 --> 13:18.130
769 seconds, 770 seconds…

13:18.214 --> 13:19.673
[doctor] We did everything we could,

13:19.757 --> 13:22.760
but the child's mother
passed away during childbirth.

13:22.843 --> 13:24.303
[tearfully] Sorry?

13:24.386 --> 13:27.056
Good heavens! How upsetting.

13:27.765 --> 13:30.267
That there is real sorrow.

13:30.851 --> 13:32.853
They've lost someone they love.

13:33.354 --> 13:36.982
781 seconds, 782 seconds, 783 seconds…

13:37.066 --> 13:39.985
[boy] Dad, you can't let go.
You just can't.

13:40.069 --> 13:41.904
[man] Of course. Dad's holding on tight.

13:41.987 --> 13:43.280
[boy] You're still there, right?

13:43.364 --> 13:45.115
-[man] I sure am!
-[boy] Did you let go?

13:45.616 --> 13:47.159
Wow! Hooray for my darling Chae-a!

13:47.243 --> 13:49.286
Hooray!

13:49.370 --> 13:51.539
Now that is real happiness.

13:51.622 --> 13:53.123
[man] Go slow! Slow down!

13:53.207 --> 13:56.377
You should try it too.
The more you try, the better you'll get.

13:56.460 --> 13:58.379
798 seconds, 799 seconds,

13:58.462 --> 13:59.964
800 seconds, 801 seconds…

14:01.173 --> 14:02.800
[woman] The thing is, ma'am,

14:02.883 --> 14:06.095
in Ka-young's case,
trying to teach her won't work.

14:06.178 --> 14:11.976
806 seconds, 807 seconds, 808 seconds,
809 seconds, 810 seconds, 811 seconds…

14:12.476 --> 14:13.769
And this

14:14.770 --> 14:15.688
is affection.

14:17.189 --> 14:18.566
Warm, isn't it?

14:18.649 --> 14:19.900
820 seconds, 821 seconds…

14:19.984 --> 14:22.027
[woman] She lacks a sense of guilt,

14:22.111 --> 14:24.405
and because she's unable
to control her rage…

14:24.488 --> 14:28.492
-Oh boy, my dear Ka-young is warm.
-[Ka-young counting indistinctly]

14:30.578 --> 14:32.079
Goodness.

14:33.038 --> 14:37.126
-My dear crybaby is so warm.
-[Ka-young counting]

14:40.296 --> 14:42.381
Goodness me. [sniffles]

14:43.340 --> 14:45.384
My stubborn darling is warm.

14:45.968 --> 14:49.263
845 seconds, 846 seconds, 847 seconds,

14:49.346 --> 14:53.517
848 seconds, 849 seconds,
850 seconds, 851 seconds…

15:01.692 --> 15:04.445
Didn't I tell you
not to take the stone out?

15:06.989 --> 15:10.743
Come hell or high water, I won't let you
take it out until tomorrow.

15:11.535 --> 15:12.411
There.

15:13.787 --> 15:16.624
Why are you doing this?
Why should I put up with it?

15:16.707 --> 15:17.750
It's uncomfortable.

15:17.833 --> 15:19.001
That's exactly it.

15:19.627 --> 15:21.045
That's what discomfort is.

15:21.629 --> 15:25.299
When people glare at you like this

15:25.382 --> 15:27.134
or narrow their eyes at you like this,

15:27.217 --> 15:29.303
it's not because they don't like you.

15:29.386 --> 15:31.555
They're just uncomfortable
around you, okay?

15:31.639 --> 15:34.224
You sure like to talk, Grandma.
You're such a pain.

15:34.892 --> 15:37.519
What do I have to do
to get out of living with you?

15:39.229 --> 15:42.483
If you study really hard
and go to college,

15:42.566 --> 15:44.652
you won't have to live with me anymore.

15:44.735 --> 15:47.071
But the thing about studying is

15:47.154 --> 15:50.908
you have to take it seriously
and be top of your class.

16:00.000 --> 16:04.338
And if you succeed, then you must attend
a prestigious college.

16:04.421 --> 16:05.631
KI KA-YOUNG
TOP ADMISSION SCORE

16:05.714 --> 16:08.258
The National University of Science
and Technology is a big deal!

16:08.342 --> 16:10.177
[Pan-geum] And once you graduate
from college,

16:10.260 --> 16:13.931
you must get a job
that pays a regular salary.

16:15.724 --> 16:17.309
Thanks! And congratulations.

16:17.393 --> 16:18.644
-Oh boy.
-[man 2] Thank you.

16:18.727 --> 16:19.770
[woman] Congratulations.

16:19.853 --> 16:22.773
-[man 1] Congratulations.
-[man 2] You've picked the perfect spot.

16:23.691 --> 16:25.609
KI KA-YOUNG
TOP ADMISSION SCORE

16:28.988 --> 16:33.575
How can she be both the town's pride
and the village fool at the same time?

16:33.659 --> 16:34.785
Honestly!

16:34.868 --> 16:35.786
At the same time?

16:36.829 --> 16:37.871
You were saying…

16:38.539 --> 16:39.999
Where did you go to college?

16:42.042 --> 16:43.544
We didn't even breach

16:44.128 --> 16:45.629
the subject of college.

16:46.255 --> 16:47.339
And more importantly,

16:47.840 --> 16:50.342
I was a little tied up at the time.

16:50.426 --> 16:54.013
Even so, a similar
educational background is important.

16:54.096 --> 16:57.057
Ka-young got into the National University
of Science and Technology

16:57.141 --> 16:58.809
-with top marks and graduated early.
-Mm.

16:59.852 --> 17:00.811
A high school grad?

17:01.979 --> 17:03.439
Uh…

17:04.481 --> 17:06.108
[humming]

17:07.317 --> 17:09.111
[Pan-geum] What was your CSAT score?

17:13.657 --> 17:17.202
-Your grandma is fuming.
-Why?

17:17.286 --> 17:18.454
Something about you

17:19.580 --> 17:21.415
doing two things at the same time.

17:21.498 --> 17:24.334
Don't ever do that again.
She seemed really disappointed.

17:26.170 --> 17:28.213
-Mm? [gasps]
-[projector whirring]

17:30.090 --> 17:31.133
[slams table]

17:33.177 --> 17:34.011
[whirring stops]

17:34.595 --> 17:36.638
-Hands off.
-[chuckles] Oh yeah?

17:39.141 --> 17:41.435
Ooh. [chuckles]

17:43.395 --> 17:45.939
-I said hands off.
-[grunts]

17:47.107 --> 17:47.983
[chuckles]

17:49.068 --> 17:49.902
[scoffs]

17:52.905 --> 17:54.740
[chuckles] You push pretty hard.

17:55.240 --> 17:56.742
[chuckles]

17:58.494 --> 18:01.914
So I guess that's how humans imagine me.

18:03.582 --> 18:05.292
THIS ANCIENT BOZO'S FIRST TIME SEEING THOR

18:05.375 --> 18:07.461
-Is that me with the hammer?
-It's not.

18:08.337 --> 18:10.089
It's not? But we have the same hair.

18:10.631 --> 18:11.465
Then… [chuckles]

18:11.548 --> 18:13.050
CAPTAIN AMERICA JUST PASSED BY

18:13.133 --> 18:15.052
-Him with the star tray--
-Not him either.

18:16.595 --> 18:17.554
Oh, I know.

18:17.638 --> 18:19.932
The one wearing the red aluminum suit…

18:20.516 --> 18:22.643
No, it's not. It's not you!

18:23.143 --> 18:25.562
They're Marv*l. You're Disn*y.

18:25.646 --> 18:27.564
You have
totally different target audiences.

18:27.648 --> 18:28.774
You and these guys…

18:29.274 --> 18:31.819
Your worlds simply cannot mix.

18:32.820 --> 18:33.987
This is all we can say.

18:35.280 --> 18:37.741
But I need to know more
to make sure we don't mix.

18:37.825 --> 18:40.202
I couldn't hear anything
through those bleeps.

18:40.285 --> 18:41.995
You may be a genie,

18:42.913 --> 18:45.207
but you will never hear
through the bleeps.

18:45.958 --> 18:47.960
Copyright is serious business.

18:48.460 --> 18:49.294
Copyright?

18:49.378 --> 18:50.504
If you must hear,

18:50.587 --> 18:54.049
you can go and seek permission
from the "Big Mouse" himself.

18:55.425 --> 18:59.221
I'm an actual genie in the flesh.
Why would I need permission?

18:59.304 --> 19:00.722
Who is this mouse anyway?

19:04.685 --> 19:06.520
-So this is the modern-day plaza?
-Yes.

19:06.603 --> 19:09.398
With three IDs,
I basically control public opinion.

19:10.524 --> 19:11.441
[sighs]

19:11.984 --> 19:13.986
-Trust me.
-Okay.

19:14.069 --> 19:15.362
[typing]

19:15.445 --> 19:17.865
[Sade] I'm honestly speechless,
so let me TL;DR this.

19:17.948 --> 19:20.033
Something outrageous happened to me.

19:20.117 --> 19:24.163
I'm a genie, but copyright stops me
from even mentioning the famous mouse.

19:24.246 --> 19:26.456
I'm the genie. This makes no sense.

19:26.540 --> 19:27.916
That's not all.

19:28.000 --> 19:31.211
They made a movie about me,
but guess what they called it. Aladdin!

19:31.712 --> 19:36.466
I've never even met an "Aladdin."
Upvote if you can relate.

19:36.550 --> 19:37.885
So what's this plaza called?

19:39.761 --> 19:40.637
[Sade] Mate Pann.

19:40.721 --> 19:41.763
"Mate Pann."

19:41.847 --> 19:45.225
See? They're already going wild
in the comments. [laughs]

19:45.309 --> 19:47.060
I told you, Master. You can count on me.

19:47.144 --> 19:48.645
-[both laugh]
-You don't say?

19:49.396 --> 19:50.522
A GENIE ON MATE PANN?

19:50.606 --> 19:51.565
GO TOUCH GRASS, BRO

19:51.648 --> 19:53.233
WE NEED ALADDIN'S SIDE OF THE STORY

19:53.317 --> 19:54.693
BIG CAP, GO SEEK HELP

19:54.776 --> 19:56.778
-But why are they criticizing me?
-Oh.

19:57.362 --> 19:59.615
-Oh. Ooh. [laughing]
-[laughing]

20:01.408 --> 20:04.119
[woman] You call this studying?
You're really going places, huh?

20:04.203 --> 20:05.829
Did you learn to read Korean?

20:07.247 --> 20:08.123
[yelps]

20:08.207 --> 20:11.877
Mr. Seo I-deuk, what are you doing here?
You said you'd chop wood for the hall.

20:11.960 --> 20:14.463
I was just getting up
to go over there now.

20:14.546 --> 20:15.881
By the way, have you eaten?

20:17.090 --> 20:18.467
Sit down while I'm being nice.

20:18.550 --> 20:20.052
The plaza is over here.

20:20.135 --> 20:20.969
Who is that?

20:21.720 --> 20:23.513
Are you two close, Mr. Seo?

20:23.597 --> 20:26.391
We have almost a millennium
to catch up on, so, you know.

20:26.475 --> 20:27.559
Never mind. Let's go.

20:27.643 --> 20:29.770
I told you to come.

20:30.395 --> 20:31.605
Come here now!

20:32.397 --> 20:35.400
-[boy] Hey, what the hell?
-[patrons clamoring]

20:35.484 --> 20:36.443
Come on!

20:37.069 --> 20:39.321
I'm going to kill
whoever pulled that crap.

20:40.113 --> 20:43.700
[boy 2 groans] I was just about
to level up, damn it.

20:45.953 --> 20:46.912
[grunts]

20:47.788 --> 20:50.082
-[all cheer]
-[exclaims]

20:50.666 --> 20:53.418
The mountains will soon be
stripped bare of trees.

20:53.502 --> 20:56.546
He's the young man staying
at my Sang-tae's guesthouse for a month,

20:56.630 --> 20:58.840
-and he's so handy. [chuckles]
-[yells]

20:58.924 --> 21:00.592
[women cheering]

21:01.468 --> 21:03.679
-[Ok-nam] Would you look at that?
-[whooping]

21:05.305 --> 21:06.890
[car engine starts]

21:10.936 --> 21:13.272
[revving]

21:18.110 --> 21:19.569
[engine revs]

21:19.653 --> 21:22.072
What's a car like that doing
in a town like this?

21:22.155 --> 21:22.990
Mm?

21:24.157 --> 21:26.743
Right. It's the psychopath's car.

21:26.827 --> 21:28.954
What? Why would you say such a thing?

21:30.497 --> 21:32.165
Hello.

21:32.249 --> 21:34.876
-I think she heard you.
-It's all right. She knows it too.

21:35.544 --> 21:36.545
Hey.

21:36.628 --> 21:38.547
Drive carefully, you!

21:38.630 --> 21:42.175
She has one of those anti-psycho
character disorders or something.

21:42.259 --> 21:45.053
Granny Park, it's called
"anti-social personality disorder."

21:45.137 --> 21:47.097
Don't forget to apply sunscreen.

21:48.181 --> 21:49.308
[Heung-rye] All right!

21:50.892 --> 21:54.354
By psychopath, do you mean
the type that kills people?

21:54.438 --> 21:56.565
She doesn't kill people, though,

21:56.648 --> 22:00.110
because we all raised her
together as a village.

22:00.193 --> 22:01.695
-And how did you raise her?
-[screams]

22:01.778 --> 22:03.447
Who are you? How'd you get here?

22:03.530 --> 22:05.949
[Heung-rye] What are you doing here?
How very strange.

22:06.033 --> 22:08.744
Right, he's her potential husband.

22:09.244 --> 22:10.579
So how did you raise her?

22:11.163 --> 22:11.997
Well,

22:12.831 --> 22:14.666
at first, it was utter chaos.

22:14.750 --> 22:16.793
Worse than anyone could've imagined.

22:16.877 --> 22:18.670
[clucking]

22:22.049 --> 22:24.634
This is "gi-yeok."

22:26.053 --> 22:27.262
This is

22:28.263 --> 22:29.306
"ni-eun."

22:31.933 --> 22:35.020
This is "di-geut."

22:37.230 --> 22:39.232
Things get a little tricky from here.

22:39.733 --> 22:40.984
Are you up for it?

22:51.161 --> 22:53.163
-[tense music plays]
-[dogs barking]

23:00.087 --> 23:01.630
-[barking stops]
-[music ends]

23:02.214 --> 23:04.549
[pleasant music plays]

23:20.107 --> 23:21.024
This girl.

23:21.108 --> 23:22.442
Dear, oh dear.

23:24.111 --> 23:26.029
Here. Try one first.

23:26.113 --> 23:28.532
You need to cut the rice cakes,
not smash them.

23:28.615 --> 23:30.408
Knife up against the rice cakes…

23:30.492 --> 23:33.370
[Heung-rye] And so,
the entire neighborhood

23:33.453 --> 23:36.540
came together to raise that tiny devil.

23:37.207 --> 23:38.583
Devil, you say?

23:38.667 --> 23:40.836
[Ok-nam] That's it. There you go.

23:40.919 --> 23:42.087
What exactly are you?

23:44.965 --> 23:46.842
[whirring]

23:52.430 --> 23:55.433
-You busy?
-I'm almost done. Can I help you?

23:56.017 --> 23:58.436
I broke a tail light while parking.

24:03.024 --> 24:05.026
[soft suspenseful music plays]

24:07.445 --> 24:10.240
You don't need to uncover
the truck bed to change it, right?

24:10.323 --> 24:11.867
My truck's loaded to the brim.

24:12.367 --> 24:13.326
It's fine.

24:13.869 --> 24:16.496
I clock out at 6:00,
so just come back before then.

24:16.580 --> 24:19.791
I'll leave it with you, then.
I'm going to eat at my mom's restaurant.

24:20.834 --> 24:22.252
[whirring]

24:29.050 --> 24:29.885
[sighs]

24:35.182 --> 24:38.018
I see you've already started. [laughs]

24:39.603 --> 24:41.980
I bought more pork belly.
Let me know if you need it.

24:42.063 --> 24:44.524
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

24:44.608 --> 24:47.527
By the way, Mr. Eom,
is the Wi-Fi here normally this bad?

24:47.611 --> 24:49.321
It's the altitude.

24:49.404 --> 24:52.407
Why not give your phones a break
and enjoy your time here?

24:53.325 --> 24:55.660
He's right.
I hear I-deuk doesn't even have a phone.

24:56.536 --> 24:59.372
I-deuk! You should stop chopping
and join us.

24:59.456 --> 25:02.042
I don't actually like cooked meat.

25:02.125 --> 25:03.210
Enjoy!

25:08.340 --> 25:09.174
GRANDMA

25:09.257 --> 25:10.383
[Pan-geum] Buy bean sprouts,

25:10.467 --> 25:13.929
those adhesive pain relief patches,
tofu, and bread.

25:15.889 --> 25:16.765
What is that?

25:16.848 --> 25:19.351
-That looks so cool.
-I told you not to come into town.

25:19.434 --> 25:20.560
Buy me one of those.

25:21.061 --> 25:22.896
-No, buy me three.
-[vehicle approaching]

25:25.649 --> 25:27.651
[dramatic music plays]

25:33.323 --> 25:34.157
Oh.

25:50.674 --> 25:54.261
I heard you brought a potential husband
from the Middle East. Is that him?

25:54.344 --> 25:57.639
Hello. He's not a potential husband.
Don't say a word.

25:57.722 --> 25:58.890
But…

25:59.891 --> 26:02.310
Don't you tell me he's not
when he clearly is!

26:04.271 --> 26:07.524
The talk of the town is
how we should plan the wedding.

26:07.607 --> 26:08.525
As for me,

26:08.608 --> 26:13.154
I'm Park Chang-sik, the village chief
here at Cheongpung Village.

26:13.238 --> 26:16.241
Here we have the youth association.
Left, Jwa Jong-heon. Right, Woo Min-jae.

26:16.324 --> 26:17.534
Say hello.

26:17.617 --> 26:18.827
Nice to meet you.

26:18.910 --> 26:21.329
Wow, you're as tall as the 63 Building.

26:21.413 --> 26:23.873
[Chang-sik laughs]
It's a nice area, isn't it?

26:23.957 --> 26:26.042
Thanks to our Ka-young here,

26:26.126 --> 26:29.337
our village has nothing to worry about
in terms of public safety.

26:31.339 --> 26:32.799
Why am I the only one talking?

26:35.051 --> 26:36.761
Am I the only one with a mouth?

26:37.304 --> 26:39.347
Am I the only one
who's happy we're meeting?

26:41.349 --> 26:43.560
Just say hello. Keep it short.

26:44.185 --> 26:45.228
Shall I, then?

26:45.979 --> 26:49.441
Uh, it appears that
you are the chieftain of this village.

26:49.941 --> 26:52.777
Nice to meet you too, Park Chang-sik.

26:57.365 --> 27:00.160
[grunts, exclaims]

27:02.996 --> 27:04.247
Ugh!

27:07.751 --> 27:10.045
-[Min-jae] Chang-sik!
-What the hell was that?

27:10.670 --> 27:13.923
Please calm down.
You'll give yourself a heart attack.

27:14.007 --> 27:17.469
What the hell did you do?
What did you do to my nose? [yells]

27:18.053 --> 27:20.555
What made you fall for me?
Am I damn irresistible?

27:20.638 --> 27:21.973
Chang-sik, use your words.

27:22.057 --> 27:23.808
I told you to let go of me!

27:27.312 --> 27:29.689
What the hell? Where'd he go?

27:32.359 --> 27:35.195
-Did he make a run for it?
-[chuckles]

27:36.613 --> 27:37.447
[sighs]

27:38.406 --> 27:40.075
[feigns screaming]

27:41.076 --> 27:42.327
What just happened?

27:43.244 --> 27:44.162
Where did he go?

27:45.121 --> 27:46.790
Where could he have gone?

27:48.124 --> 27:49.834
I wonder where he is.

27:51.211 --> 27:52.128
Damn it.

27:52.212 --> 27:54.214
CHEONGPUNGHO MART

27:54.297 --> 27:57.801
How many times must I tell you
to pay attention to the entrance display?

27:57.884 --> 27:58.843
The entrance is…

27:58.927 --> 28:01.846
"The face of our store."
But you keep leaving it bare.

28:02.347 --> 28:03.348
Don't you?

28:04.682 --> 28:06.226
[snaps fingers] Answer me, please.

28:07.268 --> 28:08.520
I'm sorry.

28:09.312 --> 28:11.815
The freight elevator
is under maintenance, so…

28:12.315 --> 28:13.400
Ms. Kang Im-seon?

28:14.401 --> 28:15.735
Does our store not have stairs?

28:16.486 --> 28:17.529
Get a move on.

28:18.571 --> 28:20.365
Right, I'll get to it now.

28:23.368 --> 28:24.327
Oh.

28:28.289 --> 28:31.584
Men don't greet each other like that
in this country. That's the rule.

28:32.252 --> 28:34.170
Huh? What is this place?

28:35.672 --> 28:36.923
And what's that?

28:40.135 --> 28:42.137
Oh! What is this place?

28:43.138 --> 28:44.347
Stay still already.

28:45.557 --> 28:48.393
-[Iblis] Whoa.
-I'm sorry, but can you see that man?

28:49.686 --> 28:52.397
Yes. He's handsome. Why do you ask?

28:53.398 --> 28:56.943
Uh, just wondered if he was only
handsome in my eyes. Thank you.

28:58.653 --> 28:59.821
[sighs]

29:01.364 --> 29:04.826
Chief Park is a former marine,
and his motto is "My pride is my success."

29:05.744 --> 29:08.955
What are you gonna do now?
You're… done for.

29:10.915 --> 29:12.500
So you think I'm handsome?

29:12.584 --> 29:14.502
I have no emotions, but I do have eyes.

29:16.254 --> 29:18.506
What don't you have? Emotions?

29:18.590 --> 29:21.551
You should be careful
not to get caught out by Min-ji.

29:21.634 --> 29:23.344
Her rules are even more intense.

29:24.179 --> 29:25.764
Wait, who is Min-ji?

29:32.520 --> 29:33.438
[woman] Excuse me.

29:34.022 --> 29:35.690
That's the ladies' restroom.

29:36.191 --> 29:37.525
I am a lady.

29:37.609 --> 29:39.944
[gasps] My apologies. I'm so sorry.

29:40.028 --> 29:41.738
It's all right. I'm used to it.

29:44.699 --> 29:47.035
-[toilet flushes]
-[door opens]

29:52.999 --> 29:54.793
[water running]

29:56.419 --> 29:57.504
[water stops running]

29:58.838 --> 30:01.257
[chuckles] I'm a woman.

30:02.467 --> 30:05.386
I know. You're the director
of Smile Dental Clinic.

30:07.388 --> 30:08.431
Do I know you?

30:09.682 --> 30:10.725
[suspenseful music plays]

30:10.809 --> 30:15.063
Wait, I remember. I saw you
when I signed the lease for my clinic.

30:15.146 --> 30:16.981
You're CEO Ryu Su-hyeon's assistant.

30:17.649 --> 30:20.151
Are you here to play golf?
Isn't this course great?

30:21.236 --> 30:22.362
I'll let him know.

30:22.904 --> 30:25.240
Mr. Ryu also owns this golf course.

30:25.323 --> 30:27.700
This too? Whoa.

30:27.784 --> 30:32.413
Even with everything he could ask for,
he's always volunteering at the food bank.

30:32.497 --> 30:35.124
He had another building
finished recently, right?

30:45.718 --> 30:49.347
[Irem] The sold units will likely
be occupied from next week.

30:49.430 --> 30:50.557
Sounds good.

30:50.640 --> 30:52.225
I'm glad to hear you're happy.

30:52.725 --> 30:55.979
The paperwork's been a nightmare for me,
but it's good that you're satisfied.

30:57.564 --> 31:01.234
Why do you still scramble for money
when you already have so much?

31:04.487 --> 31:06.155
That's the thing about being human.

31:06.739 --> 31:09.117
You don't need to go to hell
to live in hell.

31:10.326 --> 31:12.370
Having no money is hell itself.

31:13.329 --> 31:14.873
Hell doesn't suit me.

31:19.752 --> 31:20.795
[can opens]

31:20.879 --> 31:21.880
[Sade] A nose rub?

31:22.714 --> 31:24.507
At least you're still alive.

31:24.591 --> 31:26.050
For now, drink up.

31:26.551 --> 31:28.136
Being away from home is tough.

31:30.555 --> 31:33.600
-[bright music plays]
-[waves splashing]

31:40.356 --> 31:42.650
[groans, grunts]

31:43.359 --> 31:45.695
[sighs] What is this aluminum kettle?

31:47.071 --> 31:48.239
It's remarkable!

31:48.323 --> 31:51.618
You know about aluminum,
but you don't know what a can is?

31:51.701 --> 31:53.745
GOBLIN STATIONERY

31:53.828 --> 31:54.662
[sighs] Wow, this…

31:54.746 --> 31:56.581
Wait here for a short while.

31:56.664 --> 31:59.709
I'll be back as soon as
I finish my after-school helper gig.

31:59.792 --> 32:02.211
Hey. You shouldn't be helping people.

32:02.295 --> 32:05.006
You're Satan's mythical beast.
You should be ruining them.

32:05.089 --> 32:07.675
Stop the infuriating nonsense.
Wait right here.

32:09.010 --> 32:11.429
-Huh?
-[children chattering]

32:14.766 --> 32:17.018
[announcer in English on video game]
Ready, go!

32:17.101 --> 32:18.978
-[electronic music playing]
-[both grunting]

32:19.062 --> 32:21.439
-[in Korean] What is this lamp?
-[grunting]

32:21.940 --> 32:24.484
-[announcer] K.O.!
-It's amazing.

32:31.032 --> 32:32.575
-[buttons clicking]
-[grunting on game]

32:32.659 --> 32:34.869
[gasps] You're still at it?

32:35.578 --> 32:36.537
Please just go.

32:36.621 --> 32:38.039
I'd like to go too,

32:39.082 --> 32:40.416
but I just can't stop.

32:41.334 --> 32:43.169
Next time, I want to be trapped in this.

32:43.252 --> 32:46.047
-[buttons clicking]
-[grunting on game]

32:47.298 --> 32:50.635
-Ah!
-[comical music plays]

32:52.220 --> 32:54.013
[grunting continues]

32:54.889 --> 32:55.932
[groans]

32:56.015 --> 32:58.518
[muttering]

32:58.601 --> 33:00.853
-[music increases in tempo]
-[clicking intensifies]

33:00.937 --> 33:03.189
-[announcer] K.O.!
-[groans]

33:06.734 --> 33:07.610
[grunts]

33:08.277 --> 33:10.071
[exhales, laughs]

33:10.154 --> 33:12.240
[music increases in tempo]

33:12.323 --> 33:14.283
[yelps, groans]

33:15.952 --> 33:17.036
You stay right here.

33:17.120 --> 33:19.455
I'll take you on any day.

33:19.539 --> 33:20.415
[music ends]

33:33.803 --> 33:35.346
[indistinct chatter]

33:35.430 --> 33:38.349
[panting softly]

33:48.943 --> 33:50.903
[woman] Hey there. Excuse me?

33:50.987 --> 33:52.196
It's dangerous there.

33:52.280 --> 33:53.865
-[exclaims]
-[sighs]

33:56.909 --> 33:57.869
I know.

33:57.952 --> 34:00.621
Leave her alone.
She's as experienced as we are.

34:00.705 --> 34:02.290
We see her on every trail we go on.

34:02.373 --> 34:04.709
The young lady who picks up
all the trash. [laughs]

34:04.792 --> 34:06.627
Oh my, it's nice to meet you.

34:07.211 --> 34:10.131
I've heard so much about you. [chuckles]

34:10.214 --> 34:11.215
I know.

34:16.095 --> 34:17.805
[Iblis] What took you so long to get down?

34:18.931 --> 34:21.100
Why are you here?
How did you know I was here?

34:22.018 --> 34:25.063
I'm desperate. I just need 1,000 won.
It's the last time, I swear.

34:25.146 --> 34:28.441
You came all this way for 1,000 won?
Aren't you a genie?

34:28.524 --> 34:29.734
Magic yourself some money.

34:29.817 --> 34:32.278
Spirits can't make treasures
for their own use.

34:32.904 --> 34:34.947
And do you really think
I came for 1,000 won?

34:35.031 --> 34:36.532
Make your three wishes.

34:36.616 --> 34:38.785
Do it now. Right here. This instant.

34:39.452 --> 34:40.328
Or give me 1,000.

34:41.454 --> 34:42.747
So you came for 1,000 won.

34:43.706 --> 34:47.126
But if this is the last time,
that means there was also a first.

34:47.210 --> 34:49.128
-Don't tell me--
-It was Pan-geum's money.

34:50.505 --> 34:52.673
-[gasps]
-You think that makes it okay?

34:53.257 --> 34:56.594
Why are you so quick to wield a weapon?
Let's just talk this out!

34:56.677 --> 34:59.180
Get over here. You damn thief.

34:59.263 --> 35:02.183
Give it back.
Give back my grandma's money!

35:11.275 --> 35:12.193
JUST 1,000 WON!

35:12.276 --> 35:13.194
JUST 1,000 WON!

35:13.277 --> 35:14.278
JUST 1,000 WON!

35:14.362 --> 35:15.321
JUST 1,000 WON!

35:17.907 --> 35:19.283
[engine revs]

35:26.833 --> 35:29.252
[tires screeching]

35:31.337 --> 35:32.338
[sighs]

35:35.967 --> 35:36.926
Give it to me.

35:37.718 --> 35:39.137
I just want 1,000 won!

35:39.762 --> 35:40.847
You're dead meat.

35:41.556 --> 35:44.183
-[shifts gear]
-[tires screech]

35:44.267 --> 35:45.810
[Iblis] Hey, where are you going?

35:45.893 --> 35:48.312
Okay. Fine. I'll take 800,
and give you 200 change.

35:48.396 --> 35:49.480
-[car stops]
-Huh?

35:50.314 --> 35:52.066
[revving]

35:52.942 --> 35:54.610
Whoa!

35:56.237 --> 36:00.449
Hey, you insane lump of clay!

36:01.033 --> 36:03.828
Your master did this, Master?
Why would she?

36:03.911 --> 36:05.830
-[cracks]
-[both groan]

36:05.913 --> 36:07.456
I asked her for 1,000 won.

36:08.374 --> 36:12.003
-After all this, she didn't even pay up.
-Darn, my neck. 1,000 won?

36:12.086 --> 36:14.213
[exhales] It's a thing.

36:14.297 --> 36:15.798
Of course it's a thing.

36:16.465 --> 36:18.009
-I have a lot of those things.
-[gasps]

36:19.719 --> 36:21.846
Why do you have money?

36:21.929 --> 36:23.931
Because I work part-time.

36:24.432 --> 36:28.853
So your master didn't give you any money
and even ran you over with her car?

36:29.353 --> 36:30.229
So it's true.

36:30.730 --> 36:32.273
She must really be a psychopath.

36:32.356 --> 36:33.316
Yeah, that thing!

36:33.399 --> 36:37.612
What is that, and why do people keep
calling her a "path"? A path to where?

36:37.695 --> 36:39.071
PSYCHOPATH

36:39.155 --> 36:41.449
It's not like some kind of path you take.

36:42.033 --> 36:44.160
Don't be too alarmed
by the search results.

36:44.660 --> 36:45.536
Are you ready?

36:46.579 --> 36:47.413
No.

36:48.539 --> 36:50.166
They're about to level up again.

36:53.502 --> 36:55.379
If they knew it was me-- [screams]

36:56.297 --> 36:59.091
Oh. [chuckles awkwardly]
Oh, it's just you.

36:59.175 --> 37:00.801
You're getting funnier by the day.

37:00.885 --> 37:02.470
Why did the monitor switch off?

37:02.553 --> 37:03.596
Here. Take a look.

37:07.725 --> 37:08.809
Hmm?

37:10.061 --> 37:11.896
-[comical music plays]
-Huh?

37:19.111 --> 37:20.029
[yelps]

37:22.657 --> 37:23.491
[gasps]

37:24.659 --> 37:26.661
[drill whirring]

37:29.330 --> 37:32.458
How shall I explain this feeling
of intense disappointment

37:32.541 --> 37:34.085
to my dear Ki Ka-young?

37:35.169 --> 37:39.799
How am I the last person to know
that you came back from Dubai with a man?

37:40.341 --> 37:41.425
What does this jerk do?

37:41.509 --> 37:45.012
What, has he got an oil well
in his backyard or something?

37:46.472 --> 37:48.808
I'm not quite sure
what he does for a living…

37:51.352 --> 37:53.646
but he tilted the earth to hug me.

37:55.231 --> 37:58.025
-He mostly tells me to make a wish.
-A wish?

37:58.109 --> 38:00.403
[scoffs] He's clearly a cult leader.

38:00.486 --> 38:04.323
Does he mention things like the end
or corruption? Does he ask you for money?

38:04.865 --> 38:07.493
-He does.
-See? I knew it. How much?

38:08.577 --> 38:09.412
A thousand.

38:09.495 --> 38:10.705
A thousand big ones?

38:11.372 --> 38:14.083
[sighs] What a bastard. So?

38:14.166 --> 38:18.671
So I shoved him off a viewing platform,
beat him up a few times, and ran him over.

38:21.924 --> 38:24.427
-[whirring stops]
-[assistant] You're all done.

38:26.595 --> 38:29.598
Settling all that
with 10 million won is a bargain.

38:30.349 --> 38:31.684
[Min-ji] It's done. You can go.

38:36.605 --> 38:38.733
I'll go wash up
before my next appointments.

38:38.816 --> 38:39.817
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes, ma'am.

38:42.028 --> 38:45.364
By the way, why does that lady
always get in the chair to talk?

38:45.448 --> 38:47.116
She doesn't even get checked.

38:48.743 --> 38:50.453
She likes the sound of dental scaling.

38:50.536 --> 38:52.496
[gasps] Creepy.

38:54.165 --> 38:55.333
[Iblis] I should have known.

38:55.416 --> 38:58.836
I threatened to throw her from high up,
and she loved every second.

38:59.420 --> 39:01.380
This was a losing battle all along.

39:02.131 --> 39:05.134
So corrupt. She's barely human.
There's nothing for me to corrupt.

39:05.217 --> 39:08.596
She was so righteous in her past lives.
What will we do now, Master?

39:09.930 --> 39:11.515
I need to check one more thing.

39:15.019 --> 39:16.937
Whether she values the lives of others.

39:18.856 --> 39:20.941
Buy more of these aluminum kettles.

39:21.734 --> 39:23.235
The next one's to celebrate.

39:24.236 --> 39:27.239
-[tense music plays]
-[panting]

39:35.414 --> 39:37.249
[ticking]

39:38.584 --> 39:40.920
-[door opens]
-[whooshes]

39:42.838 --> 39:44.840
[tense music plays]

39:52.473 --> 39:53.891
What? Is that your lighter?

39:55.184 --> 39:57.436
Put it out.
This place is full of flammables.

39:58.020 --> 39:59.188
That comes down to you.

40:03.025 --> 40:04.902
Only you and I can put out this fire,

40:06.529 --> 40:07.488
but I won't.

40:09.365 --> 40:11.617
So the only way is if you wish for it.

40:27.383 --> 40:29.593
[music intensifies]

40:35.766 --> 40:37.852
[rattles]

40:52.032 --> 40:54.827
[screams] There's a fire! Call 911!

40:54.910 --> 40:56.036
Call 911! Oh dear!

40:56.120 --> 40:57.663
My gosh, it's a fire!

41:01.500 --> 41:03.294
How far might these flames go?

41:04.253 --> 41:05.921
Are you filming a fire insurance ad?

41:06.672 --> 41:07.506
Open this.

41:07.590 --> 41:09.592
It may engulf the entire village

41:10.176 --> 41:11.427
or an entire city.

41:13.220 --> 41:15.806
Or perhaps the entire country. [chuckles]

41:20.269 --> 41:23.314
[sighs] You just blew your chance.

41:23.814 --> 41:26.358
As soon as I'm out of here,
I'll kill you first.

41:26.442 --> 41:28.444
[tense music continues]

41:34.700 --> 41:36.035
-[music stops]
-[door closes]

41:36.118 --> 41:38.537
-[gasps]
-[rock music plays]

41:38.621 --> 41:41.499
Wait. There was another door?

41:41.582 --> 41:44.001
You should have done your research.

41:44.084 --> 41:45.586
No!

41:45.669 --> 41:46.504
Don't!

41:46.587 --> 41:49.340
Do you know how to kill jerks

41:50.674 --> 41:52.051
who just won't die?

41:52.134 --> 41:54.845
-[yelps]
-By beating them to death.

41:54.929 --> 41:56.931
[groaning]

42:02.019 --> 42:04.480
[yelps] You crazy…

42:04.563 --> 42:06.941
[yelping] That hurts so bad!

42:08.025 --> 42:10.444
The fire! Wish for the fire to be put out!

42:11.487 --> 42:13.614
Why should I? Just burn it all down.

42:14.198 --> 42:16.909
I don't care if you want
to burn the entire earth!

42:16.992 --> 42:19.203
Then why are you beating me up?

42:19.286 --> 42:21.872
Because you disrupted
my after-work routine.

42:22.414 --> 42:23.541
On a Wednesday.

42:24.166 --> 42:26.210
What? [yelping]

42:27.253 --> 42:28.462
Hold up!

42:29.505 --> 42:31.799
-[indistinct chatter]
-[siren wailing]

42:37.388 --> 42:38.681
Where is the fire?

42:40.099 --> 42:41.809
It was over there,

42:42.393 --> 42:44.436
-but it went out on its own.
-Huh?

42:44.520 --> 42:46.146
[woman] You see the scorch marks, right?

42:46.230 --> 42:48.857
I definitely saw it too.
But it went out in an instant.

42:48.941 --> 42:49.858
[Iblis yelping]

42:49.942 --> 42:53.070
First things first,
I think you should stop the assault.

42:53.153 --> 42:55.531
-[man] Over there!
-Goodness! Ms. Ki!

42:57.700 --> 42:59.493
[indistinct chatter]

43:01.161 --> 43:03.247
[officer] Ms. Ki!

43:05.207 --> 43:06.542
What on earth are you doing?

43:06.625 --> 43:08.836
You can't beat someone up like that!

43:10.129 --> 43:11.380
It's all good, sir.

43:11.463 --> 43:12.965
I'm not even a person,

43:13.966 --> 43:15.092
and I deserve it.

43:15.175 --> 43:17.386
Sir, I brought this on myself.

43:18.304 --> 43:19.763
Wait, your head.

43:19.847 --> 43:21.599
-It's dented!
-[all gasp]

43:22.433 --> 43:24.768
It's all right. It doesn't hurt at all.

43:25.311 --> 43:27.187
It'll bounce back if I flex my brain.

43:27.271 --> 43:29.315
-Wait, your arm's twisted too.
-[gasps]

43:29.398 --> 43:32.109
-[all gasp]
-[Iblis] Oh, this?

43:33.027 --> 43:35.863
It was like this when I got here.
[laughs nervously]

43:35.946 --> 43:38.741
I'm good. Please be on your way.
Thank you for your concern.

43:38.824 --> 43:40.200
So you know how to be polite?

43:41.201 --> 43:44.663
-So you knew how, but you chose not to.
-[all exclaiming]

43:45.414 --> 43:46.665
[woman] Hurry and stop her!

43:46.749 --> 43:48.292
Don't stop her!

43:48.375 --> 43:49.877
Everyone, just leave already!

43:49.960 --> 43:51.128
She hits me.

43:53.005 --> 43:54.173
And then hits me again.

43:54.673 --> 43:56.050
We're getting along great.

43:56.133 --> 43:58.886
Why are so many people getting involved?

43:58.969 --> 44:02.014
Right, welcome to the modern day,
you ancient bozo.

44:03.057 --> 44:05.976
I'll let you off because I need to go
eat gamja-tang now.

44:06.060 --> 44:08.020
If things aren't back to normal
by midnight,

44:08.103 --> 44:11.690
I'll cut you into quarters
and ship you express to whoever made you,

44:11.774 --> 44:13.108
so get moving.

44:13.192 --> 44:15.653
-I may have lost today, but I will--
-[officer gasps]

44:15.736 --> 44:17.821
-[thuds]
-[sighs]

44:20.949 --> 44:23.869
As expected, she doesn't care about
other people's lives.

44:24.703 --> 44:27.623
That was a highly successful attempt.
[chuckles smugly]

44:27.706 --> 44:31.168
You look like too much of a mess
to call it a success.

44:32.169 --> 44:33.212
It's all good.

44:34.213 --> 44:35.714
I always looked like a mess.

44:35.798 --> 44:39.176
I'm warning you. Lay a finger on me again,

44:39.259 --> 44:40.552
and I will wipe out…

44:40.636 --> 44:43.597
And to think, I made threats
that meant nothing to her. [scoffs]

44:44.682 --> 44:46.934
I underestimated a tough fight.

44:48.811 --> 44:50.562
I just need to do a little suffering.

44:51.146 --> 44:54.024
Were all of her shots aimed at your head?

44:56.819 --> 44:57.945
[laughs smugly]

44:58.028 --> 45:00.197
SA FAMILY GAMJA-TANG

45:00.823 --> 45:03.450
You went through all that fire and flood,

45:03.534 --> 45:06.078
and you're still downing gamja-tang?

45:06.161 --> 45:07.955
-It's Wednesday.
-That's right.

45:08.038 --> 45:09.748
And while we're on the topic,

45:10.457 --> 45:12.209
can't we change up the menu?

45:12.709 --> 45:13.961
The menu is fixed.

45:14.628 --> 45:16.588
This is my routine.
Our friendship routine.

45:16.672 --> 45:17.506
No, it's not.

45:17.589 --> 45:19.007
Listen carefully.

45:19.091 --> 45:21.760
In school, you beat up anyone
who messed with me, right?

45:21.844 --> 45:24.972
-Yes.
-You cared more for my grades than I did.

45:25.055 --> 45:27.474
-Right.
-Let's say your grandma dies.

45:27.558 --> 45:29.393
-Who will you call?
-The village chief.

45:30.853 --> 45:32.604
Right. And after him?

45:32.688 --> 45:34.064
-The ambulance.
-[chuckles]

45:34.148 --> 45:35.315
Correct.

45:37.025 --> 45:38.235
-And then?
-You.

45:38.318 --> 45:39.486
See?

45:39.570 --> 45:42.030
This is friendship.
Seafood stew next week. Deal?

45:44.366 --> 45:45.659
I need to eat gamja-tang.

45:45.742 --> 45:47.870
My rules and routines are absolute.

45:47.953 --> 45:50.539
Grandma is my rule,
and this is my routine.

45:50.622 --> 45:52.916
One misstep, and I'd be dangerous.

45:53.000 --> 45:56.295
Uh, we're not fighting.
Please enjoy your meals.

45:58.547 --> 45:59.840
You're wrong.

46:00.340 --> 46:01.884
You're not dangerous.

46:01.967 --> 46:04.428
You've already proven yourself.

46:05.429 --> 46:06.722
That's how it is now.

46:07.473 --> 46:10.851
But what if Grandma passes away?
Then my rules will disappear.

46:10.934 --> 46:12.060
Without my rules,

46:12.978 --> 46:13.979
I might kill someone--

46:14.062 --> 46:15.689
I'm telling you, that's not true--

46:15.772 --> 46:17.566
Don't cut me off!

46:19.026 --> 46:20.027
[sighs]

46:20.110 --> 46:22.863
-I haven't told you my workshop story yet.
-Fine, tell me.

46:23.989 --> 46:25.741
It starts with "a coffin"? Right?

46:25.824 --> 46:27.367
A coffin?

46:28.285 --> 46:30.579
Oh. I've never built a coffin before, so…

46:30.662 --> 46:32.664
Shall we start trying today, then?

46:32.748 --> 46:33.874
Two paulownia coffins.

46:33.957 --> 46:36.752
You must be preparing coffins
for your dogs.

46:37.544 --> 46:39.796
Are they elderly? How big are they?

46:40.297 --> 46:43.091
Large dogs? Or small dogs?

46:45.928 --> 46:46.845
How tall are you?

46:47.971 --> 46:50.641
She's about as tall as you are.
My grandma, not my dog.

46:50.724 --> 46:52.976
-[gasps]
-The other one is for me.

46:53.060 --> 46:56.146
-I plan to die once she passes away.
-[gasps]

46:57.523 --> 46:59.233
[Ka-young] As natural a death as possible.

46:59.316 --> 47:01.318
I'm going for something

47:01.818 --> 47:05.155
like deep-sea equipment failure
or a fall on a remote trail.

47:05.906 --> 47:06.865
Do you understand?

47:06.949 --> 47:08.700
I understand, yeah.

47:10.077 --> 47:14.122
But must you tell me every time
when I'm the one who'll be most upset?

47:14.206 --> 47:16.750
Who else would I tell?
You're my only friend.

47:16.833 --> 47:17.834
Just don't be upset.

47:17.918 --> 47:20.128
Come on, that's…

47:21.713 --> 47:24.758
[sighs] Fine.
I'll try not to let it get to me.

47:24.841 --> 47:29.012
-[sentimental music plays]
-But you would never kill someone.

47:31.682 --> 47:34.685
That kind of blind faith
is friendship, isn't it?

47:34.768 --> 47:36.603
And I'm not capable of that.

47:36.687 --> 47:37.854
You don't need to be.

47:38.981 --> 47:41.108
I still love you either way.

47:42.150 --> 47:43.235
So please,

47:43.986 --> 47:44.903
stop it.

47:46.780 --> 47:48.740
-I know.
-What the hell do you know?

47:49.283 --> 47:51.368
I don't know feelings,
but I know statistics.

47:52.035 --> 47:54.079
Every Wednesday, I eat gamja-tang.

47:54.580 --> 47:57.624
You've had gamja-tang with me
twice every month for five years.

47:57.708 --> 48:01.169
You say you don't want to come,
but you never let me eat alone.

48:01.753 --> 48:04.506
You come and erase the line
that separates me, a negative,

48:04.590 --> 48:06.300
and all the normal zeroes.

48:07.175 --> 48:08.135
Right.

48:08.760 --> 48:10.220
That's got to be love.

48:12.055 --> 48:12.973
[sighs]

48:16.351 --> 48:18.395
Keep eating. I'll get us some water.

48:24.943 --> 48:25.777
[sniffles]

48:27.237 --> 48:28.363
Hmm?

48:32.159 --> 48:33.869
-[winces]
-[Min-ji] What the…

48:33.952 --> 48:35.912
-[gasps]
-[Min-ji] What's wrong with this?

48:36.955 --> 48:38.081
Why are you here?

48:38.165 --> 48:39.041
[Min-ji] What?

48:39.666 --> 48:42.753
Don't tell me you were spying on me
from the water filter.

48:42.836 --> 48:46.173
I've straightened up the garage.
Thought you'd want to know.

48:47.007 --> 48:48.091
Damn it.

48:49.217 --> 48:51.845
Who was it? Did someone say something?

48:52.512 --> 48:54.473
We're not fighting, I swear.

48:55.807 --> 48:56.767
Enjoy your meal.

48:58.518 --> 48:59.394
Again?

49:02.856 --> 49:04.441
-Huh?
-That's 4,000 won.

49:04.941 --> 49:05.817
You're into that?

49:07.027 --> 49:08.445
I'm catering to your tastes.

49:09.696 --> 49:10.530
Follow me.

49:11.031 --> 49:13.200
-Here you are.
-I'll take that. Thank you.

49:20.415 --> 49:21.416
Take this.

49:23.085 --> 49:26.963
From now on, when only I can see you,
you wear this clip as a sign.

49:27.756 --> 49:30.550
I'm strange enough as it is.
I don't need to be any stranger.

49:30.634 --> 49:32.052
You may have no need, but I do.

49:32.886 --> 49:35.889
If you want me to wear this,
you should at least make an effort.

49:35.972 --> 49:38.475
The least you could do
is make your first wish.

49:41.853 --> 49:46.233
Why are you so hung up on those wishes?
Why do you want to kill me so badly?

49:48.235 --> 49:51.988
[sighs wearily] There's no point
telling you since you don't even remember,

49:52.698 --> 49:55.701
but it's because you trapped me
in a lamp for 983 years.

49:56.660 --> 49:57.661
Do you have proof?

50:00.664 --> 50:01.665
It was you.

50:04.167 --> 50:07.421
I watched as your flesh decayed
and your bones turned to dust.

50:07.504 --> 50:09.506
I have a handful of that dirt too.

50:11.133 --> 50:13.218
I'll admit tempting you is a challenge,

50:14.010 --> 50:17.889
but once you make a wish, you will
certainly become more corrupt. [scoffs]

50:18.473 --> 50:20.684
If the corruption of humans is guaranteed,

50:21.184 --> 50:24.688
people wouldn't have categorized me
as a psychopath or a threat.

50:25.188 --> 50:28.442
I've never even jaywalked or littered.

50:29.776 --> 50:32.070
My grandma says humans are kind beings.

50:32.154 --> 50:33.864
I am the only evil in the world.

50:36.116 --> 50:38.160
-So you're wrong.
-[chuckles softly]

50:40.495 --> 50:41.329
No.

50:42.289 --> 50:44.916
I granted the wishes of humans
for thousands of years.

50:45.542 --> 50:47.961
All humans end up corrupt
in one way or another.

50:48.837 --> 50:50.213
Then prove it to me.

50:52.174 --> 50:55.260
What in the world can I prove
in the middle of a street?

51:00.223 --> 51:01.057
Best of five.

51:02.350 --> 51:03.602
You will grant the wishes

51:03.685 --> 51:06.062
of the next five we meet here
on this road.

51:06.563 --> 51:09.024
And if more than three of them
can be corrupted,

51:09.775 --> 51:12.903
then I'll immediately make all my wishes
and die at your hands.

51:13.653 --> 51:14.571
[scoffs]

51:14.654 --> 51:16.323
My grandma never lies.

51:16.406 --> 51:18.909
-[dramatic music plays]
-[scoffs]

51:23.371 --> 51:25.749
Do you realize
what you've just put on the line?

51:26.708 --> 51:28.043
Are you really not afraid?

51:28.126 --> 51:31.922
Sorry, but I don't know how to be afraid.
So take this and do the work.

51:32.422 --> 51:34.424
In the meantime, I'll be coming up with

51:34.508 --> 51:37.511
two perfect wishes
that won't have a single flaw.

51:37.594 --> 51:38.804
Why only two wishes?

51:40.096 --> 51:41.223
I already made one.

51:41.890 --> 51:42.891
My first wish.

51:44.351 --> 51:45.185
Which is?

51:46.728 --> 51:48.313
I told you to prove it to me.

51:48.814 --> 51:50.982
Prove that humans are bound to be corrupt.

51:52.275 --> 51:53.610
This is my first wish.

51:55.195 --> 51:56.154
[scoffs]

52:00.325 --> 52:01.993
I've been tempted by you.

52:04.663 --> 52:06.623
[rock fusion music plays]

52:11.795 --> 52:12.629
[scoffs]

52:16.842 --> 52:18.844
[rock fusion music plays]
